<!--
  "Not this", already said — the ACTIVE state of svipe_heart_off_24.

  In a notification the icon is the only thing that can say whether the refusal is already in place:
  the row is four buttons wide and there is no text under them. So the heart is FILLED here, the same
  way the like button fills when the state is on, and the slash is what keeps it a refusal.

  The slash is a HOLE, not a stroke. Every icon in a Telegram notification is tinted with one colour,
  so a line drawn over a filled shape in that same colour would be invisible; cutting the diagonal
  out of the fill (one path, evenOdd, heart + a rotated band) leaves a gap that reads as a strike at
  any size and survives whatever colour the system paints it.

  Same silhouette and the same slash geometry as the outline version, so the two swap without the
  mark appearing to move.
-->
